Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Visualization, TKIVtk - 64-bit VTK ids on 32-bit Windows

IVtk_Types.hxx refused a VTK built with VTK_USE_64BIT_IDS on 32-bit Windows.
NetVtk builds VTK with 64-bit ids on every architecture, so that vtkIdType is
long long everywhere; TKIVtk's code handles its ids alike on 32 and 64 bits
(the sub-shape ids it narrows to int, it narrows on both). The guard against a
VTK with 32-bit ids on a 64-bit target stays.
---
 src/Visualization/TKIVtk/IVtk/IVtk_Types.hxx | 11 +++--------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Visualization/TKIVtk/IVtk/IVtk_Types.hxx b/src/Visualization/TKIVtk/IVtk/IVtk_Types.hxx
index 561d614..24ba24d 100644
--- a/src/Visualization/TKIVtk/IVtk/IVtk_Types.hxx
+++ b/src/Visualization/TKIVtk/IVtk/IVtk_Types.hxx
@@ -26,14 +26,9 @@
 
 #include <limits>
 
-#ifdef VTK_USE_64BIT_IDS
-  #if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(_WIN64)
-    #error "64-bit VTK library can not be linked for 32-bit target platform"
-  #endif
-#else
-  #ifdef _WIN64
-    #error "32-bit VTK library can not be linked for 64-bit target platform"
-  #endif
+// 64-bit ids work on a 32-bit target too: vtkIdType is then long long, as on a 64-bit one
+#if !defined(VTK_USE_64BIT_IDS) && defined(_WIN64)
+  #error "32-bit VTK library can not be linked for 64-bit target platform"
 #endif
 
 typedef vtkIdType   IVtk_IdType;
